<p class="meta"><span class="kicker">Paid → free</span></p>
<h1><span class="mark">20 free GitHub alternatives</span> to monthly-subscription tools</h1>
<p class="lead">Popular monthly-subscription tools, next to free GitHub tools that do a similar job. The top 8 rows are tools I actually installed, and I only rated install difficulty for the ones I installed. For the other 12 rows I only checked that the repository exists, plus its license and star count.</p>
<p class="notice">Checked on Nov 1, 2026 · License and star counts are from official GitHub info · Most of the paid tools also have a free plan. &ldquo;Alternative&rdquo; here means &ldquo;a tool that does a similar job,&rdquo; not &ldquo;the same features.&rdquo;</p>

<h2>How to read the install difficulty</h2>
<p class="legend">⭐ click only · ⭐⭐ follow the steps · ⭐⭐⭐ needs the terminal · 💀 gave up · &ldquo;Not installed yet&rdquo; = not rated</p>

<div class="tablewrap">
<table class="free">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Paid tool</th><th scope="col">Free alternative</th><th scope="col">License</th><th scope="col">Install difficulty</th><th scope="col">Watch out</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="tried"><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Paid plans of diagram tools like Lucidchart or Whimsical</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify" rel="noopener">archify</a><span class="repo">tt-a1i/archify · 92k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>Apache-2.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv">⭐⭐⭐</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>Not a standalone app. It's a skill you call from inside an AI assistant (Claude Code, Codex, etc.).</div></td></tr>
<tr class="tried"><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Paid web-scraping APIs (Firecrawl, etc.)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/Panniantong/Agent-Reach" rel="noopener">Agent-Reach</a><span class="repo">Panniantong/Agent-Reach · 107k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>MIT</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv">⭐⭐⭐</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>13 of its 17 features worked. Reddit search didn't (cause unknown). I didn't turn on the social media login features.</div></td></tr>
<tr class="tried"><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Motion graphics video tools (After Effects, etc.)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes" rel="noopener">hyperframes</a><span class="repo">heygen-com/hyperframes · 76k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>Apache-2.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv">⭐⭐⭐</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>The skill that installs with it starts by pointing you to a HeyGen (paid) login. To stay free, you have to say so yourself.</div></td></tr>
<tr class="tried"><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>v0 paid plan (build web screens with AI)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill" rel="noopener">taste-skill</a><span class="repo">Leonxlnx/taste-skill · 107k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>MIT</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv">⭐⭐⭐</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>Not a service that builds screens for you. It's a skill that changes your AI assistant's design standards. It installs into one project folder only.</div></td></tr>
<tr class="tried"><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Lovable paid plan (build web screens with AI)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable" rel="noopener">impeccable</a><span class="repo">pbakaus/impeccable · 98k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>Apache-2.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv">⭐⭐⭐</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>Also a design skill used inside an AI assistant. It can overlap with similar design skills, so check before installing.</div></td></tr>
<tr class="tried"><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Higher plans of AI coding assistants (more usage)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail" rel="noopener">ponytail</a><span class="repo">DietrichGebert/ponytail · 181k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>MIT</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv">⭐⭐⭐</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>A plugin that makes the AI assistant write less code. The usage-savings numbers are the makers' own measurements. I didn't measure them myself.</div></td></tr>
<tr class="tried"><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Paid plans of code security scanning services (Snyk, etc.)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/cloudflare/security-audit-skill" rel="noopener">security-audit-skill</a><span class="repo">cloudflare/security-audit-skill · 55k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>MIT</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv">⭐⭐⭐</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>A skill that has the AI assistant read and review code. I only installed it; I haven't run a full audit yet.</div></td></tr>
<tr class="tried"><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>ElevenLabs (AI voice)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/debpalash/VoiceStudio" rel="noopener">VoiceStudio</a><span class="repo">debpalash/VoiceStudio · 96k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>AGPL-3.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv">💀 Removed</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>It wasn't the install that stopped me, it was the result. The pronunciation was mostly right, but it didn't hold attention to the end, so I removed it.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Notion</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/AppFlowy-IO/AppFlowy" rel="noopener">AppFlowy</a><span class="repo">AppFlowy-IO/AppFlowy · 78k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>AGPL-3.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>I haven't checked whether it imports Notion pages as they are.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Zapier</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n" rel="noopener">n8n</a><span class="repo">n8n-io/n8n · 209k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>Own license (Sustainable Use)</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>To use it for free you have to run it yourself on your computer or a server. The license restricts reselling it to others as a service.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Otter.ai (transcription)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/openai/whisper" rel="noopener">Whisper</a><span class="repo">openai/whisper · 112k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>MIT</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>A transcription engine you use with commands, with no app window. It can be slow depending on your computer.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>remove.bg (background removal)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/danielgatis/rembg" rel="noopener">rembg</a><span class="repo">danielgatis/rembg · 25k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>MIT</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>A tool you use with commands, with no app window.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Figma</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/penpot/penpot" rel="noopener">Penpot</a><span class="repo">penpot/penpot · 62k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>MPL-2.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>I haven't checked whether it opens Figma files as they are.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Loom (screen recording)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio" rel="noopener">OBS Studio</a><span class="repo">obsproject/obs-studio · 79k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>GPL-2.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>It's a recording program, so there's no instant share link. You have to upload the video file separately.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>ChatGPT paid plans</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/ollama/ollama" rel="noopener">Ollama</a><span class="repo">ollama/ollama · 185k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>MIT</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>Runs AI models on your own computer. Without enough memory you can't run big models, and answer quality depends on the model you pick.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Midjourney (AI images)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI" rel="noopener">ComfyUI</a><span class="repo">Comfy-Org/ComfyUI · 144k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>GPL-3.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>Graphics card performance matters. The image model files you use with it have their own licenses to check.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Linktree paid plan (link page)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/sethcottle/littlelink" rel="noopener">LittleLink</a><span class="repo">sethcottle/littlelink · about 3k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>MIT</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>It only gives you the template for a link page. You need somewhere to host it.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Lightroom (photo editing)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/darktable-org/darktable" rel="noopener">darktable</a><span class="repo">darktable-org/darktable · 13k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>GPL-3.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>The menus are laid out differently from Lightroom. I haven't checked whether it imports Lightroom edits.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>DeepL Pro (translation)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/LibreTranslate/LibreTranslate" rel="noopener">LibreTranslate</a><span class="repo">LibreTranslate/LibreTranslate · 17k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>AGPL-3.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>To use it for free you have to run it on your own server. I haven't compared translation quality.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td data-label="Paid tool"><div>Premiere Pro (video editing)</div></td><td data-label="Free alternative"><div><a href="https://github.com/KDE/kdenlive" rel="noopener">Kdenlive</a><span class="repo">KDE/kdenlive · about 6k stars</span></div></td><td data-label="License"><div>GPL-3.0</div></td><td data-label="Difficulty"><div><span class="lv no">Not installed yet</span></div></td><td data-label="Watch out"><div>Shortcuts and menus differ from Premiere. I haven't checked whether it opens Premiere project files.</div></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>Licenses: what you need to know</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>MIT · Apache-2.0</strong>: Commercial use is fine. Keep the copyright notice.</li>
<li><strong>GPL-2.0 · GPL-3.0</strong>: Using it as is, is fine. If you modify it and distribute it to others, you must publish your modified code under the same terms.</li>
<li><strong>AGPL-3.0</strong>: Like GPL, but even offering a modified version as an online service means you must publish the modified code.</li>
<li><strong>MPL-2.0</strong>: You only have to publish the files you modified.</li>
<li><strong>n8n's own license</strong>: Using it for your own company's internal work or personal use is fine, but selling it to others as a service is restricted. Be sure to read the original text.</li>
</ul>
<p class="src">These license notes are a plain-language summary, not legal advice. Before commercial use, read the LICENSE file in each repository.</p>

